1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,944
A paper crossed. Drones flew back.

2
00:00:05,494 --> 00:00:09,062
On March 25, Pakistan delivered a fifteen-point U.S.

3
00:00:09,102 --> 00:00:13,016
ceasefire plan to Iran. According to Pakistani officials,

4
00:00:13,056 --> 00:00:20,232
it offered sanctions relief in exchange for rolling back Iran's nuclear program, limits on its missiles,

5
00:00:20,272 --> 00:00:23,146
and the reopening of the Strait of Hormuz.

6
00:00:23,186 --> 00:00:30,388
The White House declined to discuss the plan, or to say whom in Iran it was negotiating with.

7
00:00:30,738 --> 00:00:38,020
That afternoon, Iranian state media, citing an unnamed senior official, said Iran rejected the American proposal.

8
00:00:38,060 --> 00:00:43,982
It laid out five conditions of its own: an end to attacks and to the killing of its leaders,

9
00:00:44,022 --> 00:00:50,138
guarantees that the war would not happen again, reparations, an end to fighting on every front,

10
00:00:50,178 --> 00:00:54,168
and Iranian sovereignty over the Strait of Hormuz.

11
00:00:54,518 --> 00:01:02,183
Earlier that day, an Iranian drone hit the fuel depot at Kuwait International Airport, starting a large fire.

12
00:01:02,223 --> 00:01:05,152
Kuwait said it shot down six other drones.

13
00:01:05,192 --> 00:01:09,817
The fire burned for three days and was not put out until March 28.

14
00:01:09,857 --> 00:01:18,524
Debris from an intercepted missile fell near Amman, and another missile landed in a field near Hadera in Israel.

15
00:01:18,874 --> 00:01:21,755
One side said: give up what you have.

16
00:01:21,795 --> 00:01:25,151
The other said: pay for what you have done.

17
00:01:25,191 --> 00:01:29,020
Fifteen American points, five Iranian conditions.

18
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:32,020
Only one word appeared on both papers.

19
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:36,600
Hormuz. And the two countries meant opposite things by it.

20
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:40,864
One paper went out, and one paper came back.

21
00:01:41,214 --> 00:01:46,022
The radio said Pakistan had carried the American paper to Tehran.

22
00:01:46,062 --> 00:01:49,974
One way, a paper crossed. The other way, drones came.

23
00:01:50,014 --> 00:01:53,853
Her five-year-old peeked out from under the counter.

24
00:01:53,893 --> 00:01:55,941
"Mom, is that a cloud?" "No.

25
00:01:55,981 --> 00:01:59,894
Clouds are white." Talks and bombs do not take turns.

26
00:01:59,934 --> 00:02:04,860
They come together, on the same day, under the same sky.

27
00:02:05,210 --> 00:02:10,051
Kim pointed to the last line: sovereignty over the Strait of Hormuz.

28
00:02:10,091 --> 00:02:13,137
"This is not a rejection. It's a price tag.

29
00:02:13,177 --> 00:02:16,870
Iran has already been choosing which ships may pass.

30
00:02:16,910 --> 00:02:21,392
For the ships I count, it doesn't matter who holds sovereignty.

31
00:02:21,432 --> 00:02:23,330
The door just has to open."

32
00:02:23,370 --> 00:02:29,144
He smiled. It was the first time in this war Sarah had seen him smile.

33
00:02:29,444 --> 00:02:34,088
Epic Fury continues in Episode 10.
